@page "/help"
<PageTitle>How it works | QueueLess</PageTitle>
<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">YOUR GUIDE TO A SMOOTHER VISIT</span><h1>A few things worth knowing<span class="green-text">.</span></h1><p>Everything you need to make the most of your time.</p></div></div>
<div class="help-grid"><section class="panel"><Icon Name="ticket" /><h2>Join a live queue</h2><p>Create an account or sign in, then choose a service on the overview. You can have one active ticket at a time across the centre. Your ticket stays saved if you close the page.</p><p>Open My tickets to see how many visitors are waiting ahead. When the status changes to Serving, go to the counter shown on your ticket.</p></section><section class="panel"><Icon Name="calendar" /><h2>Plan an arrival</h2><p>Book a half-hour arrival slot between 09:00 and 17:30, up to seven days ahead. All times use campus time, UTC+5. Up to three upcoming reservations are allowed.</p><p>Check in between 10 minutes before and 15 minutes after your slot. Check-in creates a live ticket in arrival order. An appointment does not guarantee an exact service start time.</p></section><section class="panel"><Icon Name="clock" /><h2>Understand your wait</h2><p>Estimates use the number of visitors ahead, the current visit and the expected service duration. They are a guide, not a countdown or a guarantee.</p><p>Updates arrive automatically while connected. If the connection drops, wait for reconnection or reload the page. Your saved ticket remains in the database.</p></section><section class="panel"><Icon Name="users" /><h2>When plans change</h2><p>A waiting ticket can be cancelled from My tickets. A reservation can be cancelled from Appointments, freeing the slot for someone else. To reschedule, cancel your existing reservation and book another time.</p><p>Expired arrival windows become Missed. Active tickets from the previous campus day become No show. If a service is paused, ask the campus centre for assistance.</p></section><section class="panel"><Icon Name="monitor" /><h2>Privacy on the public display</h2><p>The live display shows only ticket numbers, service counters and aggregate queue counts. Account names and email addresses never appear on the public screen.</p><p>Operators can see visitor names when serving their queue. Only authenticated operator accounts can call visitors or change service availability.</p></section><section class="panel"><Icon Name="sliders" /><h2>Operator workflow</h2><p>Select a desk, call the next visitor, and complete the visit when finished. Mark a no-show only after checking that the visitor has not arrived. Finish the current visit before calling another.</p><p>Pausing a service stops new joins and check-ins. Existing tickets are preserved, and a current visit can still be completed. Reopen the service to resume calling.</p></section></div>
